-- title:
--   Rank-two Hecke eigenspace in the λ-adic Tate module of J₀(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion satisfies $a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, and the recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)-p\,a_{p^r}(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)$ for $p\mid M$), and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ is there a normalised eigenform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $\ell$-th coefficient agrees with $a_\ell(g)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of natural numbers, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism to $\mathbf{C}$ from the Hecke algebra of level $M$, weight $2$ and excluded set $S$, i.e. the $\mathbf{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbf{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$; assume $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $\mathcal{O}''$ be a commutative $\mathbf{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal{O}''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ into $K$. Give $J_0(M)=\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over an algebraic closure of $\mathbf{Q}$ its Hecke-module structure over $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbf{Z}[X_p : p\text{ prime}]$, and let $T=\mathrm{TateModule}\ \lambda\ (J_0(M))$ be the Hecke-stable module of sequences $x:\mathbf{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$. Then, for any $\mathbf{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ for which $a\cdot x$ has $n$-th component $(a\bmod\lambda^n)\cdot x_n$, and any ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}(\mathcal{O}''\otimes_{\mathbf{Z}_\lambda}T)$ with $TM(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$, there is a $K$-submodule $E$ of $K\otimes_{\mathcal{O}''}(\mathcal{O}''\otimes_{\mathbf{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of $K$-dimension $2$ consisting exactly of those $v$ with $(TM(X_\ell))_K\,v=\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))\,v$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\notin S$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one, rank-two half of the Eichler–Shimura construction: the system of eigenvalue equations for the good Hecke operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$) cuts out a $K$-plane inside the $\lambda$-adic Tate module of $J_0(M)$ after base change. It is the source of the two-dimensional space underlying the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to $g$, and is used in the construction of that representation, of its ordinary line at primes of good reduction, and in the comparison of the eigenplane with reduction kernels.
